l,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.40780421992050275,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.009042024400420645,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":59.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.036718123470773634,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":4.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.04998896312769193,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":16.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.49468,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Sanara MedTech Inc., a medical technology company, develops, markets, and distributes surgical solutions to physicians, hospitals, clinics, and post-acute care settings in the United States. The company offers CellerateRX Surgical, a medical hydrolysate of Type I bovine collagen indicated for the management of surgical, traumatic, and partial and full-thickness wounds, as well as first and second-degree burns. It also develops BIASURGE, a no-rinse surgical solution used for wound irrigation; FORTIFY Tissue Repair Graft(FORTIFY TRG), a freeze-dried, multi-layer small intestinal submucosa extracellular matrix sheet; BiFORM, an osteoconductive, bioactive, porous implant that allows bony ingrowth across the graft site and it can be used as a strip or molded into a putty to fill a bone defect; ACTIGEN Inductive Bone Matrix, a naturally derived, differentiated allograft matrix with robust handling properties; ALLOCYTE Plus, a human allograft cellular bone matrix containing bone-derived progenitor cells and conformable bone fibers; and TEXAGEN, a multi-layer amniotic membrane allograft used as an anatomical barrier with robust handling that can be sutured for securement. The company has a license agreement with Rochal to develop, market, and sell antimicrobial products that include BIASURGE Advanced Surgical Solution, BIAKOS Antimicrobial Wound Gel, and BIAKOS Antimicrobial Skin and Wound Cleanser for the prevention and treatment of microbes on the human body. Sanara MedTech Inc. was incorporated in 2001 and is based in Fort Worth, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Seth D. Yon | President, CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 108 people. Revenue per employee of $955K ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 41%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $48K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Sanara MedTech Inc. is a micro-cap healthcare business with a $290M market cap on $103M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +31% over the past three years and +41% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +18.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -13% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 87% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $2M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -60.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 49% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Carries a 63% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6334620334620336},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Gross margin tops the Healthcare peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Ar